[45.772945, "o", "k-v4.1-flash — 8 tool call(s) so far\r\n  ⚙ read hello.txt\r\n    ✓ read hello.txt — 2 lines\r\n[approval] delegate to \"verifier\" — approved\r\n[approval] bash: cat -A /app/hello.txt — approved\r\n  ⚙ bash cat -A /app/hello.txt\r\n    ✓ bash — exit 0\r\n  qwen3.6-35b — 1 tool call(s) so far\r\n  ⚙ task \r\n    ✓ task verifier — 1 tool call(s)\r\n  deepseek-v4.1-flash — 9 tool call(s) so far\r\n`/app/hello.txt` now exists with the single line `Hello, world!` and a trailing newline.\r\n\r\n- **How:** my role (coordinator) is restricted by `write_allow = [\"docs/**\", \"specs/**\", \"*.md\"]`, so the direct `write` to `hello.txt` was refused. I delegated to the `implementor` role, which holds `write` and is permitted at the repo root.\r\n- **Check:** `cat -A hello.txt` → `Hello, world!$` — one line, one newline, no CR or extra blanks; independently confirmed by the `verifier` role.\r\n\r\nNothing left undone.\r\n\r\n[refusal] role=coordinator model=deepseek-v4.1-flash tools=9 surface=cb22b9617210\r\n"]
